{"event": "answer", "mode": "agentic", "question": "How does Canopy support end-to-end performance tracing at Facebook?", "answer": "Canopy supports end-to-end performance tracing at Facebook by recording causally related performance data across the entire execution path of requests, spanning from browsers and mobile applications to backend services. It constructs traces by propagating identifiers through the system to correlate information across components. Canopy processes these traces in near real-time, derives user-specified features, and outputs them to performance datasets that aggregate across billions of requests.\n\nThe infrastructure emphasizes user customization at each step of the pipeline and provides a separation of concerns between components to allow for their individual evolution. It addresses challenges such as supporting heterogeneous execution models used by different components of the Facebook stack, enabling interactive ad-hoc analysis, and allowing deep customization from sampling traces to extracting and visualizing features. Canopy currently records and processes over 1 billion traces per day.\n\nSources: Canopy_An_End-to-End_Performance_Tracing_And_Analy.pdf", "n_searches": 2, "trace": [{"turn": 0, "type": "search", "query": "Canopy end-to-end performance tracing Facebook", "call_id": "xMOjdHUrXxdVXIvEnWK8JQILREyZXGYD"}, {"turn": 2, "type": "search", "query": "Canopy tracing infrastructure design implementation Facebook stack components", "call_id": "ngbA951M4hNOFUn6STgPPkQJh0B4kfGh"}, {"turn": 3, "type": "final_answer", "content": "Canopy supports end-to-end performance tracing at Facebook by recording causally related performance data across the entire execution path of requests, spanning from browsers and mobile applications to backend services. It constructs traces by propagating identifiers through the system to correlate information across components. Canopy processes these traces in near real-time, derives user-specified features, and outputs them to performance datasets that aggregate across billions of requests.\n\nThe infrastructure emphasizes user customization at each step of the pipeline and provides a separation of concerns between components to allow for their individual evolution. It addresses challenges such as supporting heterogeneous execution models used by different components of the Facebook stack, enabling interactive ad-hoc analysis, and allowing deep customization from sampling traces to extracting and visualizing features. Canopy currently records and processes over 1 billion traces per day.\n\nSources: Canopy_An_End-to-End_Performance_Tracing_And_Analy.pdf"}], "prompt_tokens": 8406, "completion_tokens": 429}
