{"event": "answer", "mode": "agentic", "question": "How does Seer localize the root cause of performance degradations in cloud microservices?", "answer": "Seer localizes root causes through a two-level tracing approach: **RPC-level distributed tracing** tracks all active requests and services to identify culprit microservices (e.g., memcached tiers or high-fanout Thrift services) causing QoS violations, while **node-level diagnostics** use tunable microbenchmarks when performance counters are disabled. The system identifies specific culprits like resource contention in caching tiers or long synchronization times in high-fanout services. It then provides the cluster manager with recommendations to avoid degradation. Seer uses lightweight distributed tracing for all services and detailed low-level hardware tracing only on-demand for likely disruptors, ensuring scalability.\n\nSources: 2019.asplos.seer.pdf", "n_searches": 2, "trace": [{"turn": 0, "type": "search", "query": "Seer localize root cause performance degradation cloud microservices", "call_id": "V37WMKs7LwTLnJ4MpctZwQ8bOURYvWlO"}, {"turn": 2, "type": "search", "query": "Seer root cause analysis microservices dependencies backpressure cascading QoS violations", "call_id": "7niGWROW5lcK5UYggdVmcOJdezQVv1jD"}, {"turn": 3, "type": "final_answer", "content": "Seer localizes root causes through a two-level tracing approach: **RPC-level distributed tracing** tracks all active requests and services to identify culprit microservices (e.g., memcached tiers or high-fanout Thrift services) causing QoS violations, while **node-level diagnostics** use tunable microbenchmarks when performance counters are disabled. The system identifies specific culprits like resource contention in caching tiers or long synchronization times in high-fanout services. It then provides the cluster manager with recommendations to avoid degradation. Seer uses lightweight distributed tracing for all services and detailed low-level hardware tracing only on-demand for likely disruptors, ensuring scalability.\n\nSources: 2019.asplos.seer.pdf"}], "prompt_tokens": 8193, "completion_tokens": 471}
