{"event": "answer", "mode": "baseline", "question": "Compare Google's Dapper and Facebook's Canopy: how do the two end-to-end tracing infrastructures differ in design and analysis capabilities?", "answer": "Based on the provided context, it is not possible to compare Google's Dapper and Facebook's Canopy. The provided text exclusively details Google's Dapper system, describing its design goals (low overhead, application-level transparency), instrumentation strategy (sampling, common libraries), data pipeline (local logs to Bigtable), and usage statistics. There is no information regarding Facebook's Canopy infrastructure or a direct comparison between the two systems in the available chunks.\n\nSources: [36356.pdf chunk 1], [36356.pdf chunk 4], [36356.pdf chunk 65], [36356.pdf chunk 19], [36356.pdf chunk 44]", "prompt_tokens": 1347, "completion_tokens": 159}
